<DocsLayout title="Themes">
  <p>MarkRust has dark and light themes. Use <strong>View → Toggle Light / Dark Appearance</strong> or <kbd>⌘⌥⇧T</kbd> on macOS (<kbd>Ctrl+Alt+Shift+T</kbd> on Windows/Linux). The conventional Reopen Closed Tab shortcut is not used for theme switching.</p>

  <h2>Dark theme</h2>
  <p>Default. Graphite background (<code>#1e1e1e</code>), light text, restrained rust accent for links and active states.</p>

  <h2>Light theme</h2>
  <p>Warm paper-white background with matching accent colors.</p>

  <h2>Syntax colors</h2>
  <p><strong>View → Highlight Colors</strong> offers Native, Ocean, and Forest palettes for editing and source syntax colors.</p>

  <h2>Configuration</h2>
  <pre><code>theme = "dark"  # or "light"</code></pre>

  <h2>Fonts</h2>
  <p>Body text uses your configured sans-serif (default Inter). Code uses Menlo/monospace. Adjust in <code>config.toml</code>:</p>
  <pre><code>font_family = "Inter"
font_size = 16</code></pre>
  <h2>Related</h2>
  <p><a href="/docs/shortcuts">Keyboard shortcuts</a> · <a href="/docs/configuration">Settings reference</a></p>
</DocsLayout>
